From: JoshuaDodds <61622842+JoshuaDodds@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:09:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] AP_Proximity: LD06: drop buffered points after a gap in
 the data

If no data arrives for more than 50ms the part built rotation and the
previous sweep are stale, so throw them away and start again.
---
 libraries/AP_Proximity/AP_Proximity_LD06.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libraries/AP_Proximity/AP_Proximity_LD06.cpp b/libraries/AP_Proximity/AP_Proximity_LD06.cpp
index 7d9157c6ef..0c697994f0 100644
--- a/libraries/AP_Proximity/AP_Proximity_LD06.cpp
+++ b/libraries/AP_Proximity/AP_Proximity_LD06.cpp
@@ -139,6 +139,12 @@ void AP_Proximity_LD06::get_readings()
 
                 const uint32_t current_ms = AP_HAL::millis();
 
+                if (current_ms - _last_distance_received_ms > PROXIMITY_LD06_TIMEOUT_MS) {
+                    // data stopped for a while: the buffered points and
+                    // the previous sweep are stale, start again with this packet
+                    _scan_count = 0;
+                    memset(_last_sweep_mm, 0, sizeof(_last_sweep_mm));
+                }
                 _last_distance_received_ms =  current_ms;
 
                 // Updates the temporary boundary and passes off the completed data
-- 
